WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:05.140
Attacus atlas - one of the world's largest
moths.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:10.800
Phyllium giganteum - ghost insects that look
like leaves.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:17.660
Dynastes hercules - one of the biggest beetles
on earth.

00:00:17.669 --> 00:00:22.210
They all make up just a small part of Adrian
Kozakiewicz's insect collection.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.720
The young breeder has found millions of Internet
fans with his videos of bugs and spiders.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.140
He says handling them is anything but icky.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:34.000
“I've always had insects at home.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.820
I'd catch them outside and then breed them.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.820
It's part of me.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:39.800
It's normal.”

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.500
The 20 year old has more than half a million
friends on facebook alone.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.440
Many of his clips have gone viral.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.400
They're now making him money.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:57.620
Adrian can earn between 200 and 400 Euro per
clip for the rights.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:02.000
The whackier the content, the more likely
it is to attract interest with agencies.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.720
His biggest hits are his selfie videos.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.080
“Normally it doesn't feel creepy.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:18.420
The big ghost insects are the exceptions since
they have claws and like to latch on near

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:19.450
your eyes.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:21.010
That's unpleasant.

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:24.340
What was also unpleasant was the world's biggest
snail.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:28.240
I had it on my face and it was too slimy.”

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.760
Adrian shoots most of his videos in this
suburban neighborhood near Karlsruhe.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:46.100
His parents' basement is kept at 24 degrees
Celsius - the preferred temperature of insects,

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.680
like the Goliath beetle.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:52.100
It can grow to 11 centimeters and usually
lives in Africa.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:58.100
Another highlight are his Australian
giant cockroaches.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:01.310
A pair of them costs 250 euros.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:06.340
Adrian owns 50 different insect and spider species.

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:07.960
Most are mantises.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:14.620
“There are species like this one that are
perfectly adapted to dead leaves.

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:19.370
There are others that also imitate living
leaves or flowers.

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:22.200
There's a huge variety of types.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.940
That's what's so fascinating about mantises.”

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:31.080
Adrian's insects are easy to care for.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.940
Mantises are carnivores that eat live locusts
and spiders.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:41.460
By contrast stick insects from Madagascar
get fresh blackberry leaves every three days.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.020
Insects make up the largest group of fauna.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:52.480
There are still many undiscovered species
living in rain forests.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:59.160
Three to four times a year, Kozakiewicz goes
to Southeast Asia to get new species - although

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.680
none that are endangered.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:05.900
Nonetheless animal right activists have complained

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.860
that he is misusing the insects as commodities and pets.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:15.460
“Many people personify insects too much.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.240
Insects have no consciousness.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:23.480
All they sense are things like temperature,
humidity and the nutrients in the creatures they eat.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:26.300
If you give them that, everything is fine.”

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:32.460
Adrian's social media success extends
beyond insect fanatics.

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:36.610
Recently, luxury Italian fashion designer
Gucci invited him to Florence to blog at an

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:38.280
exclusive fashion show.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:45.400
These thorny devil stick insects are particularly
popular among Kozakiewicz's fans because they're

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.599
both rare AND creepy.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:53.019
Every one of Adrian's videos increases interest
in insects as pets.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:57.020
“I get more and more requests every year.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:03.160
I've seen that more and more people are interested
in keeping insects, rather than, say, reptiles.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.840
Insects and other invertebrates are a new
market.”

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:12.580
Insects - for many people they're a major
turn off.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:18.580
But for Adrian Kozakiewicz, they're the most
exciting creatures in the world.

